# A tank of water, holding whatever is being simulated in it.
#
# The water is not in this file: a scene's 'medium:' is declared beside it in
# partcad.yaml, as a material. What is here is only where the subject goes --
# 100 mm above the floor, far enough from it for a block that sinks and a float
# that rises to be told apart at a glance.
#
# The subject arrives as a parameter, the way it does in the scene PartCAD ships
# ('//builtin/scene:subject'): 'pc sim' assigns the full path of the object
# whose 'simulate:' names this scene. Unlike that scene, this one says where its
# subject goes itself, so it declares no 'subject_offset' and a 'simulate:' that
# names it states no 'offset:'.
#
# Also unlike that scene, it is never empty: the subject defaults to the float,
# so the tank as declared -- what 'pc render' draws and 'pc ide view' shows -- is
# the float released in it. An empty scene is one nothing can draw.
links:
  - {{ param_subject_kind }}: "{{ param_subject }}"
    name: subject
    location: [[0, 0, 100], [0, 0, 1], 0]
